Your repository is not a backup of the CMS. It is the content store.

Structured fields use stable JSON. Long-form text uses Markdoc. Images sit beside the entry that uses them. The same input always produces the same file order, so reviews show the change that matters.

## One publish, one commit

Saves accumulate in a draft workspace where only editors see them. Publish writes everything pending — entries, sidecar files, and media together — as one change set. GitHub uses the Git Data API. GitLab uses the commits API. The local connector gives the same all-or-nothing result in a working tree.
